WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.717
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 6: My Five Senses.

2
00:00:03.797 --> 00:00:11.310
In this unit you will learn about your five senses
— seeing, hearing, smelling, tasting and touching —

3
00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:14.883
and the parts of your body you use for each one.

4
00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:22.998
You will learn describing words like soft, loud, sweet
and cold, and begin to compare things: a tree is tall,

5
00:00:23.078 --> 00:00:24.561
a building is taller.

6
00:00:24.641 --> 00:00:29.326
Most of all you will explore the
world around you, stay curious,

7
00:00:29.406 --> 00:00:33.718
and be thankful for all the wonderful things you can sense.

8
00:00:33.798 --> 00:00:39.971
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:40.051 --> 00:00:47.926
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name
the five senses: see, hear, smell, taste, touch.

10
00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:54.987
You will also point to and name the body
parts we use: eyes, ears, nose, tongue, hands.

11
00:00:55.067 --> 00:01:01.399
You will also say which sense goes with
which body part (“I see with my eyes”).

12
00:01:01.479 --> 00:01:04.402
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:04.482 --> 00:01:09.821
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: see, hear, smell, taste, touch, eyes.

14
00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:15.109
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:19.221
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:19.301 --> 00:01:24.100
The reading sequence includes Amal at
the Market and Talk about My Five Senses.

17
00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:24.964
Read actively.

18
00:01:25.044 --> 00:01:29.225
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:29.305 --> 00:01:33.239
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:33.319 --> 00:01:36.600
The first language focus is Eyes are for seeing.

21
00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:39.820
Point to your eyes and say the whole sentence.

22
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:42.830
Your eyes are the sense that helps you see.

23
00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:50.461
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:01:50.541 --> 00:01:54.463
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

25
00:01:54.543 --> 00:01:58.858
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:01:58.938 --> 00:02:02.204
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:02.284 --> 00:02:05.681
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:05.761 --> 00:02:07.254
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:14.027
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:14.107 --> 00:02:17.311
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:17.391 --> 00:02:24.905
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
